    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n14723" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">dōnārĭum</span></b> ,
		ii, n.
		donum, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>the place in a temple where the votive offerings were
			kept</i>, <i>a temple treasure-chamber</i> (perh. not
			ante-Aug.), <i><span class="en">Luc. 9, 516</span></i>;
				<i><span class="en">App. M. 1, p. 221</span></i>.
			—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Meton.</b>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b>
			<i>A temple</i>, <i>sanctuary</i>, <i>altar</i>, <i><span class="en">Verg. G. 3, 533</span></i> Serv.; <i><span class="en">Ov. F. 3,
				335</span></i>; <i><span class="en">id. Am. 2, 13,
			13</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<i>A votive offering</i>, <i><span class="en">Liv. 42,
			28</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Gell. 2, 10, 3</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Aur.
				Vict. Caes. 35</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Vulg.
				Exod. 36, 3 al.</span></i></div>
